From a11f163 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:18:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Wave 1, taps: a second tap does one thing; the menu, its
 search and the ways back
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The owner asked (2026-11-11) for a stress test of every touch and input. This is the
shell's "taps" share of wave 1, fixed once for every page: a double tap does what one
tap does and a tap aimed at a screen that is gone is dropped (core/taps.js); a new
page shows its name at once and a slow one says "Working it out…"; the menu's Find a
page box keeps what is typed, Go opens the first page listed and whole words rank
first (core/search.js); the closed menu is out of reach of keys, the open menu keeps
the page behind it still and is one step of the phone's Back; the top bar shows a
"‹" whenever Back stays in the app and the page's name is never cut; a page opened
from Needs attention or Next best action names its way back just above the one way
on at the bottom; an address that names no page says so (core/address.js) instead of
showing the Dashboard.

New: core/taps.js, core/address.js, tests/taps.test.mjs, tests/search-words.test.mjs,
tests/ways-back.test.mjs, tests/address.test.mjs, qa/shell-*.mjs (permanent checks).
core/ui/base.css: the top bar and menu rules only. index.html: the "‹" and the skip
button. tools/drive.mjs: qa.go waits while #content says aria-busy (the page's name is
painted before the page is worked out), so qa/smoke-all.mjs reads a drawn page on a
busy machine.

Simple first (the owner's rule of 2026-11-12): the named way back is drawn once, as a
plain 44 px line at the bottom where the person finishes, not a card; at the top the
bar's "‹" (spoken "Back to Needs attention") is the way back, so no second "‹ Back to
..." card sits under it. The page still ends with one card, its way on. On the
branch's newer tip (5614682) the "saved by a newer version" notice comes before the
missing-page card and counts as a draw for the tap guard and the focus.
A page that only waits for your computer (requires "pc": Backups, Change log, Statement
reader) still opens by its address and says so itself, as the gate before main checks on
the phone's site (qa/flows/static-stall.mjs "no-pc"); "soon" pages, builder's pages and
a helper's page stay "Page not found" in the household's view. All pages keeps the import
line the gate edits (pinned in tests/search-words.test.mjs).

view.js touched: modules/overview/pages/view.js (Best match by name; the address keeps
the search word).

